  "summary": "Adversarial review of the work-graph-assembly-e change-set against work-graph-integrated@2. The change-set implements the subject-assembly-is-deterministic clause comprehensively: a deterministic assembly executor (executeWorkGraphAssembly) composes admitted packet heads over an anchored base using changeset.ApplyBatch; an eligibility oracle (assemblyProducerFor) gates on v2 multi-packet Work Graphs with all packet heads admitted; assembly routing is applied unconditionally on every reachable code path — fresh produce (computeSteps), acceptance-gate retry, verification-reject revision (planVerificationRejectRevision), exact-context regeneration (exactContextRegenerationStep), and underivable-arithmetic rebuild (planUnderivableChangeSetRebuild) — never falling back to the from-scratch producer. A new admission predicate (evaluateChangeSetAssembledFrom) validates that a packetless change-set carrying assembled_from was produced by the work-graph-assembly pass and that its composition preimage exactly matches the current admitted Product occurrence and packet heads in Work Graph application-index order (D0005.C10). The standing guard (wgi-subject-assembles-from-packets) verifies machinery presence, the eligibility oracle against four fixtures, and runs six real go-test regressions covering the executor arithmetic, the retry path, both verification-reject conjunct branches, the exact-context regeneration funnel, and the underivable-arithmetic recovery. No predicate-blocking defect found: no clause is falsified, no in-force decision is violated, and no demonstrated harm is introduced on the changed surface.",
  "verdict": "accept"
